WEBVTT

asr-000033
00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:30.840
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed. Majority Leader.

asr-000034
00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:37.760
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Madam Speaker, I move to consider the proposed budget of the Energy Regulatory Commission.

asr-000034-split-2
00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:48.600
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Any objection? Hearing none, the proposed budget, the period of sponsorship, debate and interpellation of the proposed budget of the Energy Regulatory Commission is hereby open. Majority Leader.

asr-000034-split-3
00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:57.680
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Madam Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the Energy Regulatory Commission,

asr-000035
00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.980
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: namely Chairperson and CEO, Francis.

asr-000036
00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:12.340
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Juan, Commissioner Floricinda Baldo-Digal, Commissioner Marco Romeo Fuentes, Commissioner Amante Liberato, and Commissioner Paris G. Riel.

asr-000037
00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:25.680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: To the Energy Regulatory Commission family, headed by the Chairperson and the CEO, Francis Saturnino Juan, maraming salamat sa inyong pagbisita. Welcome to the House of the People.

asr-000038
00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:26.860
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000039
00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.860
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize...

asr-000040
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:36.780
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Vice Chair Arne Fuentebella from the 4th District of Camarines Sur.

asr-000041
00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:44.080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The brilliant Vice Chair of the Committee on Appropriations from the 4th District of Camarines Sur,

asr-000042
00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:49.620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the Honorable Arne Fuentebella is hereby recognized to sponsor the ERC proposed budget.

asr-000043
00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:59.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Madam Speaker. For expediency, please allow me to submit my sponsorship speech to the Committee, Madam Speaker.

asr-000046
00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I'm ready to answer the queries of our colleagues.

asr-000047
00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.120
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

asr-000049
00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:14.940
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize Representative De Jesus from Felirica Partylist.

asr-000050
00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:19.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable President De Jesus is recognized for his interpellation.

asr-000051
00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:59.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker. Of course, to the distinguished colleague of mine and to all ERC family, magandang hapon po sa atin. Madam Speaker, DOE sets energy policy.

asr-000053
00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:29.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But when an ordinary consumer asks why this amount is appearing on my electricity bill, much of the answer leads to the Energy Regulatory Commission. So let's begin with that. Does the ERC budget give it sufficient capacity to regulate a power industry that is becoming larger and substantially more complicated? Can the good sponsor confirm that the ERC total available appropriations for fiscal year 2027 are approximately

asr-000054
00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:33.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 944.1 million?

asr-000054-split-2
00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000054-split-3
00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:53.920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker and Distinguished Sponsor. Madam Speaker, compared with total available appropriations of approximately 1.83 billion in 2026, that represents a reduction of about 12.8%. Is that correct?

asr-000054-split-4
00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:56.440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Absolutely correct, Madam Speaker.

asr-000054-split-5
00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yet at the same time,

asr-000055
00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:15.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ERC is dealing with distribution and transmission rate resets, WESM interventions, net metering, microgrids, consumer refunds, and increasingly complex new technologies.

asr-000056
00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:25.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Why is ERC's resource support declining while the scope and complexity of its regulatory work are increasing?

asr-000057
00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:40.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Can you repeat, sorry, Madam Speaker?

asr-000057-split-2
00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:54.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker, nag-decline ang inyong support budget but tumaas naman the complexity of regulatory work. Kumbaga yung trabaho ninyo nadagdagan pa.

asr-000057-split-3
00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:55.380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000057-split-4
00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:59.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker. In fact, ERC

asr-000058
00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:19.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: said it originally sought approximately 1.7 billion for 2027, but the NEP provides only around 944 million, roughly 762 million or 44.7% below the agency request. Is that correct?

asr-000058-split-2
00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:21.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000058-split-3
00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:29.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So may we identify precisely what the

asr-000059
00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:42.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ERC does not get if we retain the 944 million level? What kind of software or information technology projects will not proceed? Ano ang naapektuhan dito? Because you lost over 700 million.

asr-000059-split-2
00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:59.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker. ERC has explained that the reduction principally affects MOOE and capital outlay, including funding for rate reset consultancies,

asr-000060
00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:03.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ICT modernization and additional case resolution capacity. So ito po yung pinakaapektado, Madam Speaker.

asr-000060-split-2
00:21:03.100 --> 00:21:22.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, especially the rate reset, which is most important when it comes to DUs and transmission, babagal ulit po ang pag-deliver o pagpapabilis ng kanilang reset. Madam Speaker, ito ba yun?

asr-000060-split-3
00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker. Totally agree.

asr-000060-split-4
00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:28.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, let me paraphrase my question.

asr-000061
00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:40.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many more pending CAPEX, OPEX or rate resets for private DUs as well as electric cooperatives?

asr-000064
00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:18.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker. So, in short, how many years pala yung lag natin dito, especially for the electric cooperatives? Anong year po yung ating dinidinig?

asr-000064-split-2
00:23:18.300 --> 00:23:20.800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Are we talking about CAPEX?

asr-000064-split-3
00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:28.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: CAPEX of the electric cooperatives, na since they filed, hanggang ngayon hindi pa rin natatapos.

asr-000065
00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:39.640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It's about 12 years, Madam Speaker.

asr-000065-split-2
00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:45.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Twelve years? Twelve years, so 2026 minus 12, 2014.

asr-000065-split-3
00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:47.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2013–2014.

asr-000065-split-4
00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wow.

asr-000065-split-5
00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:52.560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The oldest is 2013.

asr-000065-split-6
00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:58.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you. You know, the CAPEX, this is the problem, Madam Speaker, distinguished sponsor. As you know, Kong Arne, alam mo naman ito.

asr-000066
00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:10.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, pag na-delay yung mga CAPEX na yan, especially sa mga substation natin, sa mga upgrade natin, tatamaan lahat ng electric cooperatives at doon nasisisi na naman tayo.

asr-000067
00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:21.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, I don't blame Commissioner Bagu-Selito, but it's been there for so long, especially now that your budget has been cut by over 700 million.

asr-000068
00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:32.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, do we expect it's going to be the same thing from previous administration na mabagal pa rin ang pag-approve because of the delay?

asr-000069
00:24:33.560 --> 00:24:46.960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No, Madam Speaker. Actually, mas bumilis na rin po tayo. Actually, sa 2026, we have 170 CAPEX decisions. We're talking about the decisions.

asr-000070
00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:48.840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000071
00:24:48.840 --> 00:25:05.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, regarding the budget, that's why we are seeking additional, even just additional 200 million for consultancies because we need highly technical people, especially in the computation of the reset.

asr-000072
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:11.200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We are just talking about the electric cooperatives, wala pa po yung private, wala pa po yung NGCP.

asr-000073
00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:18.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, if you want to equip ERC for a proper regulation of our trillion.

asr-000074
00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:31.100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, in the industry, in the energy sector, we need very able people, highly technical. That's why we are asking actually for 700 million.

asr-000075
00:25:31.440 --> 00:25:40.320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, if Congress can give us even just 250 million, ERC will gladly accept it. Madam Speaker.

asr-000076
00:25:40.320 --> 00:25:48.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker. In short, I will translate that, your answer, which is very...

asr-000077
00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:59.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Very good, your answer. Actually, no, saludo sa sagot mo. If we translate that in an ordinary layman's word, wala pa rin mangyayari.

asr-000078
00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:01.080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And we are just talking about the reset.

asr-000079
00:26:01.260 --> 00:26:01.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Reset.

asr-000080
00:26:02.080 --> 00:26:03.060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's only the reset.

asr-000081
00:26:03.440 --> 00:26:04.520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi pa po yung iba lang yun.

asr-000082
00:26:04.660 --> 00:26:05.160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Isa lang po yun sa mga...

asr-000083
00:26:05.160 --> 00:26:18.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's the only thing. Iba pa yung CAPEX, iba pa yung mga OPEX natin dyan. So, again, Madam Speaker, no, tayo, lagi tayo nagre-reklamo sa mga DUs, sa transmission line, even sa ERC na...

asr-000084
00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:24.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: na mabagal sila. Eh, paano hindi babagal? Eh, kulang yung binibigay natin pondo.

asr-000085
00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:34.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But, on the other hand, I remember that Congressman Dogok and I, during one of the deliberation in committee on appropriation,

asr-000086
00:26:35.300 --> 00:26:45.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: nabigyan kayo, you were allowed to take, if I'm not mistaken, either 500 million or 700 million from your income.

asr-000087
00:26:45.260 --> 00:26:48.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama ba ako yung tinatawag natin mga...

asr-000088
00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:51.460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: collection nyo from other sources. Am I right?

asr-000089
00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:59.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, I think that's the ERC restructuring bill that already passed this chamber.

asr-000090
00:26:59.620 --> 00:27:03.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama. So, kailan pa nagsimula yun? Is it already collecting?

asr-000091
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:08.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It's still pending action by the Senate. So, dito po sa lower house.

asr-000092
00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:10.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Oh, so it's still pending. So, in short, wala pa rin yun.

asr-000093
00:27:10.420 --> 00:27:12.540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala pa rin. Ito po yung mga pinaghirapan po natin.

asr-000094
00:27:12.540 --> 00:27:17.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah, drawing pa rin pa rin yun. Anyway, I hope that will be approved at least.

asr-000095
00:27:18.080 --> 00:27:18.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pag na-approve yun...

asr-000096
00:27:18.840 --> 00:27:22.260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pag na-approve yun, medyo gaganda na yan. So, let's wait and see, no?

asr-000097
00:27:22.900 --> 00:27:26.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Siguro, Congressman Dagoque and I, pwede rin kami sumunod para makatulong,

asr-000098
00:27:26.900 --> 00:27:31.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: para malaman din nila na itong ginagawa natin para sa ating bayan.

asr-000099
00:27:31.860 --> 00:27:34.420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And I will personally support you, Congressman President.

asr-000100
00:27:34.660 --> 00:27:35.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Kong Arne.

asr-000101
00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:41.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Madam Speaker, and of course, Distinguished Spokesman,

asr-000102
00:27:41.980 --> 00:27:45.340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ERC is also proposing another way of strengthening its resources.

asr-000103
00:27:46.220 --> 00:27:48.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ERC requested special provision allowing

asr-000104
00:27:48.640 --> 00:27:54.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: it to use portion. Ito yung sinasabi ko, collection [unclear] support the regulatory mandate.

asr-000105
00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:56.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Actually, annually natin, nasa...

asr-000106
00:27:56.800 --> 00:27:58.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Magkano yung collection nyo annually?

asr-000107
00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:09.120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, in 2025, ERC reported collections of approximately 2.354 billion,

asr-000108
00:28:09.800 --> 00:28:14.220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: more than double its 1.067 billion collection target,

asr-000109
00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:18.180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and significantly higher than its annual appropriation.

asr-000110
00:28:18.840 --> 00:28:21.680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay, that's a lot of money to collect.

asr-000111
00:28:21.800 --> 00:28:25.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think we made a threshold, ata, no, Commissioner Chairman,

asr-000112
00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:31.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: na up to 700 million lang ata, regardless how much you collected.

asr-000113
00:28:31.280 --> 00:28:33.520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think they were given a cap, no?

asr-000114
00:28:34.060 --> 00:28:36.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Not 50% of the total collection.

asr-000115
00:28:36.920 --> 00:28:39.440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think may threshold sila dyan, eh, sa ginagawa.

asr-000116
00:28:40.260 --> 00:28:45.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I hope, no, the Senate will act on it para naman matugunan yung problema.

asr-000117
00:28:47.480 --> 00:28:48.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Speaker,

asr-000118
00:28:48.840 --> 00:28:54.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: let me now go to what the additional funding is supposed to accomplish.

asr-000119
00:28:54.620 --> 00:28:58.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The most obvious example is the rate reset backlog.

asr-000120
00:28:58.640 --> 00:28:59.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yun pinag-usapan natin kanina.

asr-000121
00:29:00.460 --> 00:29:05.740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ERC itself acknowledged that the distribution rate reset process

asr-000122
00:29:05.740 --> 00:29:11.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: for privately owned distribution utilities suffered more than 10 years of delay.

asr-000123
00:29:11.760 --> 00:29:12.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama ba ito?

asr-000124
00:29:14.060 --> 00:29:16.140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000125
00:29:17.720 --> 00:29:18.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Just for the record,

asr-000126
00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:22.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and for the information of this body and the public,

asr-000127
00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:30.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: how does a core regulatory function of the ERC fall more than a decade behind?

asr-000128
00:29:30.640 --> 00:29:32.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Isn't it this is your main function?

asr-000129
00:29:33.580 --> 00:29:34.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Bakit tayo masyado matagal?

asr-000130
00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:37.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 10 years ang inaabot ng reset natin.

asr-000131
00:29:38.180 --> 00:29:42.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: There were internal problems, Madam Speaker.

asr-000132
00:29:42.560 --> 00:29:46.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's why I'm with you regarding strengthening the ERC

asr-000133
00:29:46.600 --> 00:29:48.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and making its own charter.

asr-000134
00:29:48.840 --> 00:29:51.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Instead of waiting for the amendment of IPIRA,

asr-000135
00:29:51.960 --> 00:29:55.300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I think we have to make a charter for the ERC,

asr-000136
00:29:55.760 --> 00:29:57.480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: strengthen it, equip them,

asr-000137
00:29:57.840 --> 00:30:00.000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: especially ang binabantayan po.

asr-000138
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: natin ay trillion na industry

asr-000139
00:30:02.340 --> 00:30:03.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: with only

asr-000140
00:30:03.980 --> 00:30:05.980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: the budget of 900 million.

asr-000141
00:30:06.700 --> 00:30:07.820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, napakahira po.

asr-000142
00:30:08.060 --> 00:30:09.500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, kung gusto natin mabilis

asr-000143
00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:11.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: at maganda po yung function ng ERC,

asr-000144
00:30:12.260 --> 00:30:13.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I think we have to

asr-000145
00:30:13.600 --> 00:30:15.920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: restructure.

asr-000146
00:30:15.920 --> 00:30:17.620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to make the charter

asr-000147
00:30:17.620 --> 00:30:19.940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: of ERC to strengthen

asr-000148
00:30:19.940 --> 00:30:21.700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: their powers, even

asr-000149
00:30:21.700 --> 00:30:23.660
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: applying the penalties,

asr-000150
00:30:24.360 --> 00:30:25.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: not only with

asr-000151
00:30:25.760 --> 00:30:27.760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: employees, but

asr-000152
00:30:27.760 --> 00:30:29.600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: truly policing

asr-000153
00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:31.720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo ng ating pong regulation

asr-000154
00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:33.900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: sa charges sa kuryente.

asr-000155
00:30:34.300 --> 00:30:35.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000156
00:30:36.420 --> 00:30:37.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: This is a great sponsor. You know,

asr-000157
00:30:37.780 --> 00:30:39.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I'm with you with that. Kung gusto

asr-000158
00:30:39.860 --> 00:30:41.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: natin talagang bumilis

asr-000159
00:30:41.360 --> 00:30:43.880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: at maayos talaga ito, we need more

asr-000160
00:30:43.880 --> 00:30:46.120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: funding for ERC.

asr-000161
00:30:46.560 --> 00:30:47.640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But for the meantime,

asr-000162
00:30:48.520 --> 00:30:49.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: dwelling with the 900

asr-000163
00:30:49.820 --> 00:30:51.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: million funds

asr-000164
00:30:51.860 --> 00:30:53.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: natin for 2026,

asr-000165
00:30:53.580 --> 00:30:55.960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 2027, how can

asr-000166
00:30:55.960 --> 00:30:57.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: we avoid

asr-000167
00:30:57.720 --> 00:30:59.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: yung 10 years na

asr-000168
00:30:59.500 --> 00:31:01.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: madesisyonan, despite

asr-000169
00:31:01.820 --> 00:31:03.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the fact na 900 million lang yun?

asr-000170
00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:05.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, anong gagawin natin?

asr-000171
00:31:05.560 --> 00:31:07.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, for example, we have no choice anymore.

asr-000172
00:31:08.500 --> 00:31:10.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, ano yung mga

asr-000173
