Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and if indeed there was

asr-002165
02:06:22.340 --> 02:06:24.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: lapse on the part

asr-002166
02:06:24.760 --> 02:06:26.260
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of the Rules Secretariat,

asr-002167
02:06:26.260 --> 02:06:28.660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: they will duly approve.

asr-002168
02:06:28.680 --> 02:06:29.180
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I apologize.

asr-002169
02:06:29.580 --> 02:06:31.360
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: No, Madam Speaker, I cannot accept that.

asr-002170
02:06:31.440 --> 02:06:32.640
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I want you to make a ruling now.

asr-002171
02:06:32.740 --> 02:06:33.960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: You can consult, we can suspend,

asr-002172
02:06:34.100 --> 02:06:35.720
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: you can consult with the Majority Leader,

asr-002173
02:06:35.840 --> 02:06:37.880
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: with the Speaker, but I will not accept that.

asr-002174
02:06:37.940 --> 02:06:39.120
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: You have to make a ruling now.

asr-002175
02:06:39.660 --> 02:06:41.020
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Well, basically, the rules,

asr-002176
02:06:41.500 --> 02:06:43.780
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Honorable Chanko, applies to members

asr-002177
02:06:43.780 --> 02:06:44.540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of the House.

asr-002178
02:06:45.140 --> 02:06:47.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, so can I let my photographer and videographer

asr-002179
02:06:47.680 --> 02:06:48.180
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: in now?

asr-002180
02:06:50.120 --> 02:06:50.800
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pardon me?

asr-002181
02:06:51.500 --> 02:06:53.880
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kung it applies to the members

asr-002182
02:06:53.880 --> 02:06:55.980
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: of the House, papasukin nyo na po ngayon

asr-002183
02:06:55.980 --> 02:06:57.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: yung photographer ko at videographer.

asr-002184
02:06:58.680 --> 02:07:01.340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yeah, session suspended.

asr-002185
02:07:01.340 --> 02:07:03.320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: So, just to align,

asr-002186
02:07:03.440 --> 02:07:04.340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: just for the record,

asr-002187
02:07:04.680 --> 02:07:06.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: we will just validate the name of your staff,

asr-002188
02:07:06.620 --> 02:07:08.460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: we will confer with the rules on what happened

asr-002189
02:07:08.460 --> 02:07:10.540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and then we will resume session.

asr-002190
02:07:10.660 --> 02:07:11.940
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session suspended for a few minutes.

asr-002191
02:07:11.940 --> 02:07:12.540
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-002207
02:13:56.580 --> 02:13:57.800
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed.

asr-002208
02:13:58.680 --> 02:14:06.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: After discussion with the Secretariat of the Rules Committee,

asr-002209
02:14:06.520 --> 02:14:10.160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the ruling of the presiding officer says,

asr-002210
02:14:10.500 --> 02:14:19.080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: all congressional staff with valid ID are allowed to take pictures and photos of their principal

asr-002211
02:14:19.080 --> 02:14:22.120
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: as long as they will not disrupt the plenary.

asr-002212
02:14:23.080 --> 02:14:24.240
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-002213
02:14:24.600 --> 02:14:27.860
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So, does it mean to say, papayagan na pong pumasok yung staff ko right now?

asr-002214
02:14:27.860 --> 02:14:32.300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes, they will be admitted as long as they present their official ID

asr-002215
02:14:32.300 --> 02:14:35.380
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and that they're plantilia staff of the members of Congress.

asr-002216
02:14:35.380 --> 02:14:39.700
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, pangalawa pong parliamentary inquiry, Madam Speaker.

asr-002217
02:14:40.100 --> 02:14:41.960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I'm glad that you're the one presiding today.

asr-002218
02:14:42.560 --> 02:14:48.920
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Noong pong lunes, you called me out of order because of section 105.

asr-002219
02:14:50.540 --> 02:14:56.780
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ang sabi niyo po doon, I cannot request to reopen the budget

asr-002220
02:14:56.780 --> 02:14:59.960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: of the house because

asr-002221
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:28.220
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: At ang sinayot niyo po noon is when a measure, report, or motion is approved, adopted, or lost, a member who voted, this is the important word, who voted with the majority may move for its reconsideration on the same or succeeding session.

asr-002222
02:15:28.220 --> 02:15:36.200
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ang sabi niyo po noon, since wala po ako doon, hindi ako bumoto, kaya hindi ako pwede mag-reconsider.

asr-002223
02:15:36.760 --> 02:15:45.420
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: But this section should be related to this section on voting. It cannot stand alone.

asr-002224
02:15:46.300 --> 02:15:54.600
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And what does the voting say? Voting says we vote either ace or nace or nominal voting.

asr-002225
02:15:54.600 --> 02:15:58.200
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: There are two modes of voting. Ace and nace.

asr-002226
02:15:58.220 --> 02:16:05.360
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: And nominal voting. So hanapin ko lang po kung ano yung exactong rule.

asr-002227
02:16:07.360 --> 02:16:16.760
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Rule 16, Section 117, Manner of Voting. So hindi ko nang buhahabain, papahabain, no?

asr-002228
02:16:17.440 --> 02:16:24.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: The speaker shall arise and state the motion or request that is being put to vote in a clear, precise, simple language.

asr-002229
02:16:24.520 --> 02:16:33.260
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: The speaker shall say as many as in favor as the question may be, say aye.

asr-002230
02:16:34.260 --> 02:16:40.460
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: After the affirmative vote is counted, the speaker shall say as many as opposed, say nay.

asr-002231
02:16:41.460 --> 02:16:45.960
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Sumunod po noon, nominal voting. Hindi ko nababasahin, hindi effecto.

asr-002232
02:16:45.960 --> 02:16:54.200
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ang sabi niyo po doon, kaya hindi po pwedeng pagbigyan yung reconsideration ko, is because,

asr-002233
02:16:54.520 --> 02:16:57.300
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I did not vote. Okay?

asr-002234
02:16:58.040 --> 02:17:04.300
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I will make it clear, and gusto niyo balikan natin yung video, hindi po umabot sa voting.

asr-002235
02:17:04.980 --> 02:17:10.680
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Meron lang pong nag-motion to terminate, merong nag-agree, pero hindi po umabot sa voting.

asr-002236
02:17:10.680 --> 02:17:16.500
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: At hindi niyo po pwede idahilan na dahil walang tumutol, ay hindi na umabot sa voting.

asr-002237
02:17:17.060 --> 02:17:24.420
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Because, pag second reading, when you request for the approval of the measure, even if no one objects,

asr-002238
02:17:24.520 --> 02:17:26.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: you go through voting.

asr-002239
02:17:27.900 --> 02:17:34.140
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So dito, hindi umabot sa voting, hindi applicable po yung sinasabi niyong section. Maliwanag po yan.

asr-002240
02:17:37.140 --> 02:17:41.620
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: In response to the query of the Hon. Chanko, if I may,

asr-002241
02:17:42.760 --> 02:17:49.480
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Section 105 refers to the motion for reconsideration as put forward by any member of this House.

asr-002242
02:17:50.040 --> 02:17:54.260
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The presiding officer stands by a ruling,

asr-002243
02:17:54.520 --> 02:18:01.700
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: that a motion for reconsideration shall only be allowed to a member who voted with the majority.

asr-002244
02:18:02.420 --> 02:18:08.280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With regard to your query whether an ayes and nays or a nominal voting was conducted,

asr-002245
02:18:08.620 --> 02:18:12.280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the ayes and nays is done when we approve a measure on second reading.

asr-002246
02:18:13.080 --> 02:18:21.280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: In this case, it was a motion from the minority jointly done with the majority to terminate the period of interpolation.

asr-002247
02:18:21.920 --> 02:18:24.200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: In other words, we are on the period of

asr-002248
02:18:24.200 --> 02:18:26.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: sponsorship debate and interpellation.

asr-002249
02:18:26.760 --> 02:18:32.880
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: And motions with regards to this are done by basic motions, not with an ayes and nays.

asr-002250
02:18:32.880 --> 02:18:37.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: No, but Madam Speaker, Section 105 refers to voting.

asr-002251
02:18:37.520 --> 02:18:39.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So the question is, nagdaroon ba ng...

asr-002252
02:18:39.520 --> 02:18:41.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Section 105 refers to motions for reconsideration.

asr-002253
02:18:41.520 --> 02:18:43.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, with regards to voting.

asr-002254
02:18:43.520 --> 02:18:45.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Tignan niyo po yung section.

asr-002255
02:18:45.520 --> 02:18:51.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: If I may, Your Honor, allow me to read Section 105.

asr-002256
02:18:51.520 --> 02:18:55.000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: When a measure, report, or motion is approved,

asr-002259
02:18:55.000 --> 02:18:57.320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: adopted or lost,

asr-002261
02:18:57.520 --> 02:19:04.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and in this case, it's a motion to approve the motion to terminate the period of interpolation

asr-002262
02:19:04.520 --> 02:19:07.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and the proposed budget of a certain agency.

asr-002263
02:19:07.520 --> 02:19:09.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, was there voting?

asr-002264
02:19:09.520 --> 02:19:15.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes, because the presiding officer said, is there any objection?

asr-002265
02:19:15.520 --> 02:19:23.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It's a motion to terminate the period of interpolation and the proposed budget

asr-002266
02:19:23.520 --> 02:19:26.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of whichever agency was discussed.

asr-002267
02:19:26.520 --> 02:19:31.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yes, pero sa pag nagbubotohan tayo ng second reading, kahit walang mag-object,

asr-002268
02:19:31.520 --> 02:19:33.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: you still call the eisen-nace.

asr-002269
02:19:33.520 --> 02:19:36.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: That is for second reading, Honorable Chanko.

asr-002270
02:19:36.520 --> 02:19:40.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, if you will insist, Madam Speaker, let us go by your theory.

asr-002271
02:19:40.520 --> 02:19:42.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I am present here today.

asr-002272
02:19:42.520 --> 02:19:44.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With due courtesy, Honorable Chanko.

asr-002273
02:19:44.520 --> 02:19:48.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It is not my theory, it is the rules of the House of Representatives,

asr-002274
02:19:48.520 --> 02:19:52.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and I'm citing Section 105, which refers to motions for reconsideration.

asr-002275
02:19:52.520 --> 02:19:55.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: It is your interpretation of the rules.

asr-002276
02:19:55.520 --> 02:19:59.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It is not my interpretation, it is the rules,

asr-002277
02:19:59.520 --> 02:20:02.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and as presiding officer, that is what we stand for.

asr-002278
02:20:02.520 --> 02:20:06.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, sige ha, sundan natin yung list.

asr-002279
02:20:06.520 --> 02:20:09.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With due courtesy, Your Honor, actually what you could have done

asr-002280
02:20:09.520 --> 02:20:13.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: was that when the presiding officer ruled you out of order,

asr-002281
02:20:13.520 --> 02:20:17.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: you could have appealed, and we were waiting for you to appeal,

asr-002282
02:20:17.520 --> 02:20:20.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: then you will be given five seconds to explain your appeal.

asr-002283
02:20:20.520 --> 02:20:21.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Five minutes, Madam Speaker.

asr-002284
02:20:21.520 --> 02:20:22.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Pardon me, Your Honor?

asr-002285
02:20:22.520 --> 02:20:24.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Five minutes, not five seconds.

asr-002286
02:20:24.520 --> 02:20:26.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Five minutes, I stand corrected.

asr-002287
02:20:26.520 --> 02:20:30.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: And after that appeal, if your appeal will be lost, then we can put it into a vote.

asr-002288
02:20:30.520 --> 02:20:36.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Unfortunately, during that time, you did not appeal and waived that right.

asr-002289
02:20:36.520 --> 02:20:40.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, yes, Madam Speaker, I will explain why I did not appeal at that time.

asr-002290
02:20:40.520 --> 02:20:42.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pinabayaan ko nila lang yun eh.

asr-002291
02:20:42.520 --> 02:20:46.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Kasi kahit naman mag-appeal ako, alam naman natin dito, sagasaan dito.

asr-002292
02:20:46.520 --> 02:20:48.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Hindi naman ako mananalo sa appeal.

asr-002293
02:20:48.520 --> 02:20:49.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pero sobra na yung nangyayari.

asr-002294
02:20:49.520 --> 02:20:50.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Ano nangyayari?

asr-002295
02:20:50.520 --> 02:20:52.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Yung staff ko kanina hindi pinapasok.

asr-002296
02:20:52.520 --> 02:20:56.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Nung nagbilangan tayo ng boto dito, pinalabas nila 221.

asr-002297
02:20:56.520 --> 02:20:59.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Eh wala pa nga ang kalahat yung nakaupo dito. Eh sobra na.

asr-002298
02:20:59.520 --> 02:21:01.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, I will go with your reasoning.

asr-002299
02:21:01.520 --> 02:21:03.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Let me correct that for the record, Your Honor.

asr-002300
02:21:03.520 --> 02:21:06.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: After conferring with our staff,

asr-002301
02:21:06.520 --> 02:21:14.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: we were informed that they deny the allegation na hindi pinapasok ang staff mo.

asr-002302
02:21:14.520 --> 02:21:18.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: But the allegation that they were not allowed

asr-002303
02:21:18.520 --> 02:21:23.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to take photos and videos was because of the internal agreement or internal rules.

asr-002304
02:21:23.520 --> 02:21:29.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: That's why you have those white placards or how do you call that?

asr-002305
02:21:29.520 --> 02:21:31.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Signages in the gallery.

asr-002306
02:21:31.520 --> 02:21:34.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: No videos, pictures taken or whatsoever.

asr-002307
02:21:34.520 --> 02:21:39.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: But the chair has already ruled that that will be allowed as long as they are official,

asr-002308
02:21:39.520 --> 02:21:45.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: plantilia, staff members of the office, of your office.

asr-002309
02:21:45.520 --> 02:21:46.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, let's go back.

asr-002310
02:21:46.520 --> 02:21:47.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Pinalampas ko na lang yun. Pero...

asr-002311
02:21:48.520 --> 02:21:51.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Just for the record, can we request the Secretary General

asr-002312
02:21:51.520 --> 02:21:54.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to retrieve the 200 plus that the Honorable Chanko is referring to?

asr-002313
02:21:54.520 --> 02:21:55.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Okay.

asr-002314
02:21:55.520 --> 02:21:57.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Is this in relation to your...

asr-002315
02:21:57.520 --> 02:22:03.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: No, it was in relation to the Speaker calling for a roll call at that time. Okay?

asr-002316
02:22:03.520 --> 02:22:07.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes, we have the record.

asr-002317
02:22:07.520 --> 02:22:12.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It includes 21 members who were present at the Senate Impeachment Court.

asr-002318
02:22:12.520 --> 02:22:13.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Yes.

asr-002319
02:22:13.520 --> 02:22:17.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It also included members who were on official business similar to the time that

asr-002320
02:22:17.520 --> 02:22:22.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: during the past weeks when you were on official business since you were in Italy,

asr-002321
02:22:22.520 --> 02:22:28.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: your presence has also been recorded as present because you were on official business.

asr-002322
02:22:28.520 --> 02:22:30.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay, okay, Madam Speaker.

asr-002323
02:22:30.520 --> 02:22:31.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Let us just go with your ruling.

asr-002324
02:22:31.520 --> 02:22:33.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Let us go with your ruling.

asr-002325
02:22:33.520 --> 02:22:37.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, if that is your ruling, I was present today.

asr-002326
02:22:37.520 --> 02:22:42.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: I voted with the approval of all agencies tackled today.

asr-002327
02:22:42.520 --> 02:22:46.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: So if we go by your ruling, do you mean to say I can move now to reconsider all these?

asr-002328
02:22:46.520 --> 02:22:50.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Do you want to test your ruling? Let's test it now.

asr-002329
02:22:50.520 --> 02:22:53.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Would you like to reconsider the proposed...

asr-002330
02:22:53.520 --> 02:22:55.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: All, all, all, even those in the morning.

asr-002331
02:22:55.520 --> 02:22:59.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: If that is your ruling, if that is your ruling, then we can test your ruling, Madam Speaker.

asr-002332
02:22:59.520 --> 02:23:05.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: We are actually tackling the proposed budget on a per-agency basis.

asr-002333
02:23:05.520 --> 02:23:07.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, but you said per day.

asr-002334
02:23:07.520 --> 02:23:09.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, but you said per day.

asr-002335
02:23:09.520 --> 02:23:10.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Madam Speaker, you said per day.

asr-002336
02:23:10.520 --> 02:23:15.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hence, if there is no objection, the period of interpolation for that proposed agency

asr-002337
02:23:15.520 --> 02:23:17.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: is terminated.

asr-002338
02:23:17.520 --> 02:23:24.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: But if the Honorable Chanko is so willing to request for the reopening of any agency

asr-002339
02:23:24.520 --> 02:23:27.520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to which he was present, then we will consider that.

asr-002340
02:23:27.520 --> 02:23:28.520
Rep. Tobias "Toby" M. Tiangco: Okay.

asr-002341
02:23:28.520 --> 02:23:30.520
Rep. Aniela Bianca D. Tolentino: Madam Speaker, I move to suspend session for today.

asr-002342
02:23:30.520 --> 02:23:32.520
